0282: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0283:     """
0284:     Repaint regions from T-shaped control markers, erase the markers, and optionally rotate based on a color-9 L-marker.
0285: 
0286:     Input structure:
0287:     - The grid is a mosaic of monochrome regions.
0288:     - Color 1 forms T-shaped control markers on region boundaries.
0289:     - Some controls use three singleton color-1 pixels around a colored center; that center is a literal replacement color.
0290:     - An optional 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker triggers 90-degree rotation of the output.
0291: 
0292:     Rule:
0293:     - For a color-1 T marker, the single stem points at the destination region to repaint.
0294:     - The two diagonal cells behind the stem identify the source region; the destination gets that source region's original color.
0295:     - For a colored-center T marker, the same stem identifies the destination, but the center color is the replacement.
0296:     - All marker cells are filled with the final color of the source-side region.
0297:     - A 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker controls rotation: ┐ (corner top-right) → CCW 90°, ┌ (corner top-left) → CW 90°.
0298: 
0299:     Key insight:
0300:     - The stem chooses what changes, while the two diagonals behind the stem choose where the marker itself belongs.
